>            getting made into antholes when they should?

I suspect that this is referring to the fact that if the type of ant
that would populate the anthole is genocided/extinct, then the anthole
will be created with random monsters.  You'll still get a room with
food and the message "You enter an anthole!" though.  Most of the
special rooms have a check for whether there are any of the appropriate
monster left before creating the room, so I added a similar one for
antholes in NH4.  Antholes are rare (I actually bumped up the probability
of creation to test the fix more easily), but I didn't find anything
to suggest that that is not intentional.

You could also get strange behavior in temples, morgues, and throne
rooms if all of the appropriate monsters are gone, although that takes
a little more doing since there is a much wider variety of monsters
for those -- I would guess that would mostly come up for extinctionists
who do their dirty work before heading to the castle.  Also, if the
monsters for the special room become extinct while creating the room,
then the remainder of the room would be filled with random monsters, which
is also a little weird.  I didn't address either of those.

As an unrelated thing, wouldn't it make sense for cockatrice nests to
contain both cockatrices and chickatrices?

